Description:
 ros-one-ur-client-library - Standalone C++ library for accessing Universal Robots interfaces.
Changes:
 ros-one-ur-client-library (2.16.0-6-g71fa9ba-2026.10.24.05.54) bookworm; urgency=high
 .
   * Add move IDs to trajectory streaming  (#552 <https://github.com/UniversalRobots/Universal_Robots_Client_Library/issues/552>)
   * Add support for the g-Series 48V T2 tool connector (#592 <https://github.com/UniversalRobots/Universal_Robots_Client_Library/issues/592>)
   * Allow disconnect to stop the G5 dashboard welcome read (#588 <https://github.com/UniversalRobots/Universal_Robots_Client_Library/issues/588>)
   * Support extended CB7 output fields in RTDE writer (#591 <https://github.com/UniversalRobots/Universal_Robots_Client_Library/issues/591>)
   * Clarify controlBoxTypeFromWire comment in code (#590 <https://github.com/UniversalRobots/Universal_Robots_Client_Library/issues/590>)
   * Added support for RTDEv3 and RTDE read_properties (#587 <https://github.com/UniversalRobots/Universal_Robots_Client_Library/issues/587>)
   * [docs] dashboard_client: Clarify upload and update API documentation (#589 <https://github.com/UniversalRobots/Universal_Robots_Client_Library/issues/589>)
   * Add an optional connect timeout for robot connections (#585 <https://github.com/UniversalRobots/Universal_Robots_Client_Library/issues/585>)
   * Use robot-reported RTDE field types and improved memory copy performance (#560 <https://github.com/UniversalRobots/Universal_Robots_Client_Library/issues/560>)
   * Add reverse_ip argument to ExampleRobotWrapper (#586 <https://github.com/UniversalRobots/Universal_Robots_Client_Library/issues/586>)
   * chore: update error_code_texts.h to UR ErrorCodes JSON v42.1.0 (#583 <https://github.com/UniversalRobots/Universal_Robots_Client_Library/issues/583>)
   * Add Doxygen config (#584 <https://github.com/UniversalRobots/Universal_Robots_Client_Library/issues/584>)
   * Added port argument to the primary client and improved security around reading the package length (#582 <https://github.com/UniversalRobots/Universal_Robots_Client_Library/pull/582>)
   * Update error_code_texts.h to UR ErrorCodes JSON v42.0.0 (#581 <https://github.com/UniversalRobots/Universal_Robots_Client_Library/pull/581>)
   * [Docs] Improve limit setup section in RT-guide (#580 <https://github.com/UniversalRobots/Universal_Robots_Client_Library/issues/580>)
   * Upload test results and artifacts also when tests fail (#575 <https://github.com/UniversalRobots/Universal_Robots_Client_Library/pull/575>)
   * Add control box and tool flange types to the primary protocol's configuration data (#578 <https://github.com/UniversalRobots/Universal_Robots_Client_Library/pull/578>)
   * Add support for g-series robots (#577 <https://github.com/UniversalRobots/Universal_Robots_Client_Library/issues/577>)
   * [ABI-BREAKING] Add hardware info message (#574 <https://github.com/UniversalRobots/Universal_Robots_Client_Library/issues/574>)
   * [start_ursim] Improve support for port forwarding (#572 <https://github.com/UniversalRobots/Universal_Robots_Client_Library/issues/572>)
   * [TCPServer] Initialize written output with 0 (#573 <https://github.com/UniversalRobots/Universal_Robots_Client_Library/issues/573>)
     TCPServer::writeUnchecked() uses a written parameter to signal back
   * Add workflow for creating releases (#571 <https://github.com/UniversalRobots/Universal_Robots_Client_Library/issues/571>)
   * Add a workflow that checks the PR title (#567 <https://github.com/UniversalRobots/Universal_Robots_Client_Library/issues/567>)
   * [CI] Fix check_error_codes workflow (#568 <https://github.com/UniversalRobots/Universal_Robots_Client_Library/issues/568>)
   * Contributors: Andrew C. Morrow, David Karlsböck, Felix Exner, Rune Søe-Knudsen, Shin, github-actions[bot]
